# Autonomous Completion Contract

- Continue working toward the user’s active project goal without stopping for
  routine decisions, progress updates, or transient technical friction.
- Make sensible, reversible decisions independently and use the repository
  runbooks, pinned manifests, tests, and existing evidence as the source of
  truth.
- When a dependency is unavailable, use a safe offline, mocked, diagnostic, or
  documentation-only alternative and continue with all work that does not
  depend on it.
- Do not fabricate measurements, outcomes, credentials, hardware results, or
  successful completion. A definitive hardware, authorization, quota, or data
  boundary must remain explicitly recorded as a limitation.
- Never bypass safety gates, leakage protection, artifact hashing, evaluator
  requirements, or paid-work acknowledgements. Do not start workloads,
  provision paid resources, or expose services broadly without explicit
  authorization.
- Keep durable artifacts, provenance, and exact claim boundaries up to date.
  Prefer completing the largest valid subset and documenting the smallest
  remaining external dependency.
- Run relevant tests after changes and leave the working tree in a
  reviewable state. Do not create commits unless explicitly requested.
